---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import DirectoryTable from "../../components/DirectoryTable.astro";
import directory from "../../data/directory.json";

// A generated listing page whose `.md` twin (dist/directory.md) twins.py writes
// from /reference/directory/ plus an inventory of the sites below, so Base emits
// the default `/directory.md` twin link rather than `twin={null}`.
//
// SCOPE, published on the page because the numbers do not speak for themselves:
// the mirror behind this directory holds more files than the directory scores.
// gen_directory.entries() takes only rows whose mirrored file splits into at
// least one `# Title` / `Source:` page, because a file with no page grammar
// cannot be scored page-by-page. The counts below are the mirror snapshot the
// build read; site/tests/test_directory_pages.py fails if they drift from it.
const CATALOGUED = 766;   // rows in outputs/llms-full/manifest.json
const FETCHED = 608;      // of those, status "ok" with a local file
const { sites, count, generated } = directory;
const unscored = FETCHED - count;
const GRADES = ["A", "B", "C", "D", "F"];
const spread = GRADES.map((g) => [g, sites.filter((s) => s.grade === g).length]);
const pages = sites.reduce((n, s) => n + s.pages, 0);
const title = "The directory of known llms files";
const description = `${count} of the ${FETCHED} mirrored llms-full.txt files — the ones that split into pages — each scored against the /ldo rubric by llms_lint (S2 and H8 excluded). Recorded ${generated}.`;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} route="/directory/">
  <p>
    The <strong>{count}</strong> mirrored <code>llms-full.txt</code> files that split into at
    least one page, scored against the <a href="/reference/attributes/">attribute rubric</a>
    by <code>llms_lint</code> — out of <strong>{FETCHED}</strong> we fetched and
    <strong>{CATALOGUED}</strong> we know of. {pages.toLocaleString("en-US")} pages between the
    scored ones, on <strong>{generated}</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The other {unscored} fetched files carry no <code>Source:</code> page grammar for the linter
    to walk, so they are not graded here. That exclusion is not neutral — a file with no page
    grammar fails the content-fidelity attributes it is never charged for — so the spread below
    describes the scorable subset, not the population:
    <a href="/reference/directory/">what the directory measures</a> says which files are excluded
    and why. Two attributes are not scored on any card either — <code>S2</code> (an
    <code>llms-small.txt</code> sibling) and <code>H8</code> (a <code>manifest.json</code>) —
    because one mirrored file cannot answer them.
  </p>
  <p>
    The grade is the linter's arithmetic, not an opinion:
    {spread.map(([g, n], i) => (<>{i > 0 && ", "}<strong>{g}</strong> {n}</>))}.
    <a href="/reference/directory/">What the grade means</a>, and why we link each
    source's own file instead of republishing the text we mirrored.
  </p>

  <DirectoryTable sites={sites} />

  <p>
    <a href="/reference/directory/">How the directory is scored</a> ·
    <a href="/reference/attributes/">The attribute rubric</a> ·
    <a href="/reference/spec/">The spec</a> ·
    <a href="/reference/directory/#how-a-site-is-corrected-or-removed">Correct or remove an entry</a>
  </p>
</Base>
